      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© Georg Thieme Verlag KG Stuttgart · New York.",
        "AbstractText": "Group discussions with obese teenagers and parents with obese children are the empirical basis of this research project. The results indicate that 'being fat' is primarily a social experience. Consequently, preventive measures to inhibit unhealthy lifestyle habits fail to go into sufficient depth. Overweight adolescents call for equality; they demand a more equal treatment in social interactions and relations."
      },
